[[File:MidRimSectors-BMF18.jpg|thumb|250px|The sectors of the Mid Rim]]
A '''sector''', also known as a '''star sector''',<ref name="Eye" /> was an area of [[Realspace|space]] or land framed by an artificial, conventional boundary.

A [[planet]]ary sector contained a number of [[Star system|solar systems]].<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> Sectors were also regional political divisions.<ref name="Dawn">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> [[The galaxy]] was divided into a little over 1,000 sectors.<ref name="Complete Vehicles 2018">[[Star Wars: Complete Vehicles (2018)|''Star Wars: Complete Vehicles'' (2018)]]</ref> Under the rule of the [[Galactic Empire]] there existed 1,024 individual regional sectors<ref name="BMF 20">{{BuildFalconCite|20|Starship Fact File}}</ref> which were placed under the authority of a [[Moff]], or sector [[governor]]. Several sectors could be regrouped into an [[Oversector]] governed by a [[Grand Moff]].<ref name="Tarkin" />

The boundaries of sectors overseen by [[ISB Supervisor|supervisors]] of the [[Imperial Security Bureau]] were created by [[Major]] [[Lio Partagaz]].<ref name="Announcement">{{Andor|Announcement}}</ref>

Specific surface areas of a planetary body could also be partitioned into sectors. During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] divided their territory on [[Anaxes]] into sectors, including [[Sector One]].<ref name="Bad Batch">{{TCW|The Bad Batch (episode)}}</ref> The [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] world of [[Batuu]] transported refuse from [[Black Spire Outpost]] to [[Sector 3263827]].<ref name="Galaxy's Edge">{{GEAttr|Sector 3263827}}</ref>

